A.1.13. {"problem": "A dry-run verify still runs the effect `set target.verified: true`, but the stage stays `built`. The request now has verified=true without having been deployed or probed. This contradicts the glossary ('a deployment a person has verified in use, after its probes passed') and the pairing of the `verified` flag with the `verified` stage in the invariants and the rule `only-a-person-deliveryrequest-verified`. The verified-requests-* invariants only check the stage, so they cannot catch it. Nothing separates a dry run from a real verification.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, action verify (effects) and glossary 'verified'", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.1.14. {"problem": "The verified=true set by a dry run is never cleared. The request can later be previewed again or deployed, and `record_deployment` resets only `probes_passed`, not `verified`. A deployed request can therefore show verified=true with no probes run and no real verification, and anything that reads `verified` will treat an unverified deployment as verified.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, verify vs record_deployment effects and the built/done matrix", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.1.15. {"problem": "The dry-run precondition `target.stage == 'built'` skips the `probes-passed` check, and it also lets a build whose harness failed (e.g. fixture R2) be 'verified'. The `deployed` and `probes-passed` preconditions are weakened without any equivalent guard such as `harness_ok`. Their reasons and the `verify` description still say a deployment with passing probes is required.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, verify preconditions `deployed` and `probes-passed`", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.1.16. {"problem": "The weakened `deployed` precondition keeps its old source, the interview quote 'agree with all recommendations' (L5) that backed the original rule. That quote cannot support the new dry-run exception. The diff also marks the preconditions and the matrix cell as proposed, but the post-change file still shows them as confirmed. Declaration status and evidence are inconsistent with the diff.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, verify preconditions and transitions built.verify", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
