A.2.14. {"problem": "The glossary entry 'verified' ('A deployment a person has verified in use, after its probes passed there') and the invariants verified-requests-were-deployed and verified-requests-passed-their-probes say verification needs a deployment and passed probes. The change now allows verify without either, because probes-passed is waived for stage 'built'. The invariants only hold because the dry run keeps stage 'built', yet verified: true is set anyway. The 'verified' meaning in the glossary and the action description is no longer consistent.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, glossary.verified and invariants verified-requests-were-deployed / verified-requests-passed-their-probes", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.2.15. {"problem": "The 'built' stage is also reached on a redeploy preview, where the request is already deployed (done → preview → built). The new 'or target.stage == built' clause waives the probes-passed check in that case too, not only for a first-time dry run. A previously deployed request whose probes failed can be marked verified from 'built'. The clause is broader than the stated intent of a built, not yet deployed request.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, verify preconditions deployed and probes-passed", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
